  "scenario_brief": "The last train out of Miskatonic Halt runs nearly empty tonight: five passengers in five carriages, and the cult may have people among them. They mean to finish a working before the train reaches the coast. At every stop they get rid of whatever could give them away, so search a carriage before you move on. The doors open one stop at a time; wait by the far door if you want the next stop sooner.\n\nWhat to look for. A passenger is a cultist if they match any of these.\nKeyholder: Carries the brass Tesseract key. There is only one.\nCourier: Was in the Archive, wants the Codex, and carries no ward charm.\nDevotee: Has three or more marked clues.\n\nName an innocent, or leave a cultist unnamed, and the ritual completes. You will not get a second chance.\n\nMake the call on the case board in the last carriage, after the last stop.",
  "show_scenario_brief": "once",
  "_note_brief": "invented: plan silent (brief wording around the verbatim profile texts and briefText; place name Miskatonic Halt)",

